@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il33-readings`
IMPORT `nii-il33-fixtures`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-a1-ages`
IMPORT `nii-s2a-residence`
IMPORT `isl-benefit-gate`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests: the Income Support Law's gate. Row IL-33. Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew
-- (lines 78-126, 138, 163-167, 267, 273 of the Law's deposited text) before the run.
-- Dates: the month asked about begins 1 March 2026 unless said; the claim was submitted in January 2026.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Fixtures`

unemployed MEANS `registered at the employment service as unemployed and offered no suitable work, section 2(a)(2)`

GIVEN grounds IS A LIST OF `A ground of entitlement under section 2(a) of the Income Support Law`
      first   IS A BOOLEAN
      res24   IS A BOOLEAN
      pension IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
`facts: grounds` grounds `, First Schedule ground` first `, resident 24 months` res24 `, pension` pension MEANS
    `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law` WITH
        `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`  IS grounds
        `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`                IS first
        `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`  IS res24
        `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`   IS pension
        `is in an institution maintained wholly at the expense of the State or another named body, section 3(1)` IS FALSE
        `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`     IS FALSE
        `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`              IS FALSE
        `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)` IS FALSE
        `is barred by section 3C (a conviction for a terror offence)`               IS FALSE
        `stayed outside Israel on every day of the month, section 14A(a)`           IS FALSE

-- The ordinary claimant's facts: registered unemployed, resident 24 months, no pension.
ordinary MEANS `facts: grounds` (LIST unemployed) `, First Schedule ground` FALSE `, resident 24 months` TRUE `, pension` FALSE

GIVEN f IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
GIVETH A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
f `with section 3(1) barring` MEANS
    `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law` WITH
        `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`  IS f's `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`
        `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`                IS f's `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`
        `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law` IS f's `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law`
        `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`  IS f's `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`
        `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`   IS f's `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`
        `is in an institution maintained wholly at the expense of the State or another named body, section 3(1)` IS TRUE
        `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`     IS f's `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`
        `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`              IS f's `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`
        `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)` IS f's `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)`
        `is barred by section 3C (a conviction for a terror offence)`               IS f's `is barred by section 3C (a conviction for a terror offence)`
        `stayed outside Israel on every day of the month, section 14A(a)`           IS f's `stayed outside Israel on every day of the month, section 14A(a)`

GIVEN f IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
GIVETH A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
f `with section 3C barring` MEANS
    `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law` WITH
        `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`  IS f's `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`
        `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`                IS f's `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`
        `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law` IS f's `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law`
        `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`  IS f's `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`
        `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`   IS f's `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`
        `is in an institution maintained wholly at the expense of the State or another named body, section 3(1)` IS f's `is in an institution maintained wholly at the expense of the State or another named body, section 3(1)`
        `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`     IS f's `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`
        `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`              IS f's `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`
        `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)` IS f's `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)`
        `is barred by section 3C (a conviction for a terror offence)`               IS TRUE
        `stayed outside Israel on every day of the month, section 14A(a)`           IS f's `stayed outside Israel on every day of the month, section 14A(a)`

GIVEN f IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
GIVETH A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
f `abroad all month` MEANS
    `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law` WITH
        `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`  IS f's `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`
        `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`                IS f's `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`
        `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law` IS f's `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law`
        `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`  IS f's `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`
        `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`   IS f's `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`
        `is in an institution maintained wholly at the expense of the State or another named body, section 3(1)` IS f's `is in an institution maintained wholly at the expense of the State or another named body, section 3(1)`
        `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`     IS f's `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`
        `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`              IS f's `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`
        `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)` IS f's `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)`
        `is barred by section 3C (a conviction for a terror offence)`               IS f's `is barred by section 3C (a conviction for a terror offence)`
        `stayed outside Israel on every day of the month, section 14A(a)`           IS TRUE

GIVEN f IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
GIVETH A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
f `in the Area` MEANS
    `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law` WITH
        `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`  IS f's `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`
        `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`                IS f's `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`
        `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law` IS TRUE
        `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`  IS f's `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`
        `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`   IS f's `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`
        `is in an institution maintained wholly at the expense of the State or another named body, section 3(1)` IS f's `is in an institution maintained wholly at the expense of the State or another named body, section 3(1)`
        `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`     IS f's `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`
        `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`              IS f's `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`
        `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)` IS f's `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)`
        `is barred by section 3C (a conviction for a terror offence)`               IS f's `is barred by section 3C (a conviction for a terror offence)`
        `stayed outside Israel on every day of the month, section 14A(a)`           IS f's `stayed outside Israel on every day of the month, section 14A(a)`

GIVEN b IS A NUMBER
      i IS A NUMBER
      ds IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      claim IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The money of a month under the Income Support Law`
`money: without income` b `, income` i `, determining sum` ds `, claim month` claim MEANS
    `The money of a month under the Income Support Law` WITH
        `the benefit for a person without income, from the Second Schedule`                          IS b
        `the income, computed under sections 9 to 12`                                                IS i
        `the determining sum that applies to the claimant under section 7(a), if regulations fix one` IS ds
        `the first day of the month in which the claim was submitted`                                IS claim

GIVEN dob IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
`a resident man born on` dob MEANS `a person` "Claimant" `born` dob `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` dob) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`

GIVEN dob IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
`a resident woman born on` dob MEANS `a person` "Claimant" `born` dob `who is` `female` `with` (`a resident since` dob) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`

ron MEANS `a resident man born on` (YMD 1980 1 1)
March MEANS YMD 2026 3 1
January MEANS YMD 2026 1 1

§ `Tests — section 2: who is entitled`

-- Ron, 46, a resident, registered unemployed, resident for 24 months, no pension: entitled.
#ASSERT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` ron `with` ordinary `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- 25 years: a man born 1 March 2001 turns 25 on 1 March 2026; one born 2 March 2001 does not.
#ASSERT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` (`a resident man born on` (YMD 2001 3 1)) `with` ordinary `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT NOT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` (`a resident man born on` (YMD 2001 3 2)) `with` ordinary `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- Under 25 but a ground of the First Schedule: entitled.
#ASSERT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` (`a resident man born on` (YMD 2005 3 2)) `with` (`facts: grounds` EMPTY `, First Schedule ground` TRUE `, resident 24 months` TRUE `, pension` FALSE) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- No ground at all, below retirement age (a man born 1 January 1980 reaches 67 in 2047): not entitled.
#ASSERT NOT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` ron `with` (`facts: grounds` EMPTY `, First Schedule ground` FALSE `, resident 24 months` TRUE `, pension` FALSE) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- The ground of reaching the retirement age (2)(a)(4): a man born 1 January 1958 reached 67 on 1 January 2025;
-- one born 1 January 1960 reaches it in 2027.
#ASSERT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` (`a resident man born on` (YMD 1958 1 1)) `with` (`facts: grounds` EMPTY `, First Schedule ground` FALSE `, resident 24 months` TRUE `, pension` FALSE) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT NOT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` (`a resident man born on` (YMD 1960 1 1)) `with` (`facts: grounds` EMPTY `, First Schedule ground` FALSE `, resident 24 months` TRUE `, pension` FALSE) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- 24 consecutive months of residence: required, unless a pension is paid.
#ASSERT NOT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` ron `with` (`facts: grounds` (LIST unemployed) `, First Schedule ground` FALSE `, resident 24 months` FALSE `, pension` FALSE) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` ron `with` (`facts: grounds` (LIST unemployed) `, First Schedule ground` FALSE `, resident 24 months` FALSE `, pension` TRUE) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- A visitor (B/2) who lives in Israel is not a resident (s 2A): not entitled. A resident of the Area is.
#ASSERT NOT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` (`a person` "Visitor" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a person living in Israel under` `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `with` ordinary `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` (`a person` "Area" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` `a person living abroad` `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `with` (ordinary `in the Area`) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

§ `Tests — section 3: who is not entitled`

#ASSERT NOT `ISL s 2 to 4 — entitled to a benefit:` ron `with` (ordinary `with section 3(1) barring`) `and a spouse` NOTHING `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT NOT `ISL s 2 to 4 — entitled to a benefit:` ron `with` (ordinary `with section 3C barring`) `and a spouse` NOTHING `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `ISL s 2 to 4 — entitled to a benefit:` ron `with` ordinary `and a spouse` NOTHING `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

§ `Tests — section 4(a): a couple`

-- Ron and Dana: Ron is entitled only if the spouse meets the s 2 conditions. Dana, born 1982, registered unemployed:
-- she meets them if she has resided 24 months.
#ASSERT `ISL s 2 to 4 — entitled to a benefit:` ron `with` ordinary `and a spouse` (JUST (`A claimant under the Income Support Law` WITH `the person` IS `a resident woman born on` (YMD 1982 1 1), `the facts` IS ordinary)) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT NOT `ISL s 2 to 4 — entitled to a benefit:` ron `with` ordinary `and a spouse` (JUST (`A claimant under the Income Support Law` WITH `the person` IS `a resident woman born on` (YMD 1982 1 1), `the facts` IS (`facts: grounds` (LIST unemployed) `, First Schedule ground` FALSE `, resident 24 months` FALSE `, pension` FALSE))) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- The spouse's s 3 bar is not a condition of s 4(a) (it names s 2 only): Ron stays entitled.
#ASSERT `ISL s 2 to 4 — entitled to a benefit:` ron `with` ordinary `and a spouse` (JUST (`A claimant under the Income Support Law` WITH `the person` IS `a resident woman born on` (YMD 1982 1 1), `the facts` IS (ordinary `with section 3(1) barring`))) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

§ `Tests — what is paid for the month (ss 5(b), 7, 8, 14(a), 14A(a))`

-- Ron, 46, with 3000 for a person without income and 1000 of income: 3000 - 1000 = 2000. He is under 55 and
-- paid no pension, so s 7 does not apply (s 7(c), the benefit of s 5(a)(2)(a)), even with a determining sum.
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` ron `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` ron `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` (JUST 2500) `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 2000
-- Income not below the benefit for a person without income: nothing.
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` ron `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 3500 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 0
-- A man born 1 January 1966, 60, at least 55: s 7 applies (not retirement age, not a couple). Determining sum 2500:
-- income 1000: the lesser of 3000 - 1000 = 2000 and 2500 - 1000 = 1500: 1500. Income 2400: the lesser of 600 and
-- 100: 100. Income 2500 (not below): 0.
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` (`a resident man born on` (YMD 1966 1 1)) `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` (JUST 2500) `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` (`a resident man born on` (YMD 1966 1 1)) `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 2400 `, determining sum` (JUST 2500) `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` (`a resident man born on` (YMD 1966 1 1)) `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 2500 `, determining sum` (JUST 2500) `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 0
-- A couple: s 7 does not apply (s 7(c)): 3000 - 1000.
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` (`a resident man born on` (YMD 1966 1 1)) `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` (JUST 2500) `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` TRUE EQUALS 2000
-- The same man with a pension: at 60 he is also within the 55-and-over rule; s 7 applies as before.
-- s 8: a benefit under 6 new shekels is not paid unless a pension is paid: 1005.99 - 1000 = 5.99 -> 0; 1006 - 1000 = 6 -> 6.
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` ron `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 1005.99 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` ron `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 1006 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` ron `with` (`facts: grounds` (LIST unemployed) `, First Schedule ground` FALSE `, resident 24 months` TRUE `, pension` TRUE) `and` (`money: without income` 1005.99 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 5.99
-- s 14(a): payment starts on the 1st of the month of the claim. Claim in March 2026: March is paid, February not.
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` ron `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` March) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, of` ron `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` March) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 0
-- s 14A(a): a month spent wholly outside Israel: nothing.
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` ron `with` (ordinary `abroad all month`) `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 0

§ `Tests — a benefit is paid for the month`

#ASSERT `ISL — a benefit is paid for the month beginning` March `to` ron `with` ordinary `, a spouse` NOTHING `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` January) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- Not entitled (s 3(1)): nothing paid whatever the sums.
#ASSERT NOT `ISL — a benefit is paid for the month beginning` March `to` ron `with` (ordinary `with section 3(1) barring`) `, a spouse` NOTHING `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` January) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- Entitled but the income takes the whole benefit.
#ASSERT NOT `ISL — a benefit is paid for the month beginning` March `to` ron `with` ordinary `, a spouse` NOTHING `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 3000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` January) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- A woman born in 1990 (the Retirement Age Law, s 3: 65 years, not reached) with the ground registered unemployment:
-- entitled; and s 7(c) asks whether she has reached the retirement age, which it answers, so the amount is answered:
-- 3000 less 1000 of income, no determining sum.
#ASSERT `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` (`a resident woman born on` (YMD 1990 1 1)) `with` ordinary `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` March `, of` (`a resident woman born on` (YMD 1990 1 1)) `with` ordinary `and` (`money: without income` 3000 `, income` 1000 `, determining sum` NOTHING `, claim month` January) `, a couple:` FALSE EQUALS 2000
